{
 "id": "ink_selective",
 "label": "Selective Colour (Inks)",
 "category": "Colour Correction",
 "version": 1,
 "blurb": "The printer's way to fine tune colour, as in photo editors: for each colour family (reds, yellows, greens, cyans, blues, magentas) and for whites, neutrals and blacks, add or take away cyan, magenta, yellow and black ink. Relative changes the ink that is already there, Absolute adds a fixed amount. By default it cleans up reds and deepens blue skies a little. Different from Selective Colour, which picks one colour and turns its hue.",
